          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            Crystallographic groups (also: “space groups”) are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Iso(D)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+groups"} Euclidean groups
            containing a full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+%28discrete+subgroup%29"} lattice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi d
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}^d \subset \mathbb{R}^D
            and having a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
            %em point group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \coloneqq S/\mathbb{Z}^D
            (a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+rotation+group"} finite rotation group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo ∈
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \in {2,3}
            these appear in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+groups"} symmetry groups
            of (idealized)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystals"} crystals
          %p
            The use of crystallographic groups for the study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystals"} crystals
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Hilton03"} Hilton 1903
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "crystal#Engel86"} Engel 1986
            = succeed "/the" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein+geometry"} Klein geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erlanger+program"} Erlanger program
            (see for instance
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "Erlanger+program#Weyl38"} Weyl 1938
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Erlanger+program#GruenbaumShephard10"} Grünbaum &amp; Shephard 2010
          %p
            Concretely, the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+orbifold"} quotient orbifold
            of the space of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+vectors"} wave vectors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/momenta"} momenta
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystal"} crystal
            lattice by the (dual)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystallographic+group"} crystallographic group
            is the
            = succeed "(-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+matter+theory"} condensed matter theory
            is formulated (see for instance the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron+energy+bands"} electron energy bands
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+bundle"} valence bundle
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases"} K-theory classification of topological phases
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong crystallographic group
            or
            %strong space group
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+group"} Euclidean group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+in+a+vector+space"} lattice
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of that lattice. In other words, it is a subgroup of the automorphism group of the lattice that contains all the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translations"} translations
            by elements of the lattice itself.
          %p
            Equivalently, a crystallographic group on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Iso(E)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            (its
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+group"} Euclidean group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+%28discrete+subgroup%29"} lattice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \subset E \subset Iso(E)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation+group"} translations
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+subgroup"} normal subgroup
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \subset S
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+group"} point group
            of the crystallographic group, is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi N
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \coloneqq S/N \;\subset\; O(E)
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
          %p
            In short, a crystallographic groups is exhibited by an inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequences"} short exact sequences
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group"}> non-abelian
            )
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
          #eq:CrystallographicInclusionOfShortExactSequences.maruku-equation
